<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span id="p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR ltx_centering undefined">\thetitle</span>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_centering">
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:144%;">Supplementary Material 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithmic details of the visual token importance scores and the hierarchical visual token pruning strategy are shown in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Visualization of Attention Heatmap</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further demonstrate the behavioral characteristics of the vision encoder across different layer depths and to motivate the selection of the middle-layer index set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}=\{l_{7},l_{8},l_{9},l_{10}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}=\{l_{7},l_{8},l_{9},l_{10}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to compute visual token importance scores in our method, we present additional examples from the MME benchmark showing the attention heatmaps at different layers of the vision encoder in LLaVA-v1.5-7B.
As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> to Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, from layer 7 to layer 10, the visual tokens corresponding to the main objects in the image exhibit higher brightness, indicating higher attention weights.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Visualization of POPE Examples</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text, we hypothesize that our local retaining in HIVTP can mitigate hallucination in VLMs due to reduced visual uncertainty. To validate this hypothesis, we visualize more examples from the POPE benchmark to illustrate the difference between HIVTP (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=50</annotation></semantics></math>, w/o local retaining) and HIVTP (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=25</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=2</annotation></semantics></math>). As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> to Figure <a href="#A1.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ A.3 Visualization of POPE Examples ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ HIVTP: A Training-Free Method to Improve VLMs Efficiency via Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning Using Middle-Layer-Based Importance Score" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, HIVTP (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=50</annotation></semantics></math>, w/o local retaining) causes the dropping of large contiguous regions (as indicated by the purple ellipse), which increases visual uncertainty and results in hallucination across all these examples. In contrast, HIVTP (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=25</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=2</annotation></semantics></math>), due to the use of local retaining, prevents the dropping of large contiguous regions and avoids hallucination. This visualization result supports our hypothesis that local retaining can mitigate hallucination by reducing visual uncertainty.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Visual Token Importance Scores</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="algorithm1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Complete collection of multi-head attention maps from all vision encoder layers <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>;
Indices of all visual encoder layers <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(L)</annotation></semantics></math>;
Middle layers range parameters <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,q</annotation></semantics></math>;
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"><span id="algorithm1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
Visual token importance scores </span><math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐒</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 1.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Index of selected middle layers:
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 2.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{s}=\{l_{m},\dots,l_{m+q}\}\subseteq\mathcal{I}(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">⊆</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{s}=\{l_{m},\dots,l_{m+q}\}\subseteq\mathcal{I}(L)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 3.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.5.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">each <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in L_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in L_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="algorithm1.6.5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 4.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Extract attention maps from </span><math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">: </span><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{(l,H)}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times(N+1)\times(N+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{(l,H)}\in\mathbb{R}^{H\times(N+1)\times(N+1)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.6.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> ;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 6.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">end for</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 7.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Compute importance scores:
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 8.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{(H)}=\frac{1}{|L_{s}|}\sum_{l\in L_{s}}\mathbf{A}^{(l,H)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">s</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{(H)}=\frac{1}{|L_{s}|}\sum_{l\in L_{s}}\mathbf{A}^{(l,H)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 9.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.10.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathbf{A}}=\frac{1}{H}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{(H)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">h</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi></msubsup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathbf{A}}=\frac{1}{H}\sum_{h=1}^{H}\bar{\mathbf{A}}^{(H)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> ;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 10.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.11.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{S}=\frac{1}{N+1}\sum_{j=0}^{N}\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{j,1:}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐒</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}=\frac{1}{N+1}\sum_{j=0}^{N}\bar{\mathbf{A}}_{j,1:}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> ;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;"> 11.</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm1.6.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">return</span><span id="algorithm1.6.12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.12.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;"><math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math></em>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.13" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Hierarchical Visual Token Pruning</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="algorithm2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Visual token importance scores <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times 1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
Visual tokens output by penultimate vison encoder layer <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"><span id="algorithm2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><span id="algorithm2.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
Retained visual tokens </span><math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{v}^{\text{retained}}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times d_{v}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.800em">𝐙</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">v</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">retained</mtext></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{v}^{\text{retained}}\in\mathbb{R}^{p\times d_{v}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.6.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
